# The fork of Idris's compiler (compiler/idris) carries the change of
# upstream/53-constructor-implicit-mark/pull-request.diff: the elaborator
# binds an implicit argument a pattern leaves out as an as-pattern the
# clause records as left to unification, and the compile-time tree splits it
# after the field whose pattern fixes it, not before
# (upstream/52-relevant-implicit-split's order). Main.idr's `v1` (a relevant
# implicit of `C1`) and `v3` (an erased implicit of `C2`, at quantity 0) are
# covering under `%default total`; the pinned, unpatched Idris reports each
# not covering, with two missing cases, and refuses the module. When a
# re-sync brings upstream's fix, the report, its PINS.md entry and this test
# go (upstream/README.md).
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/tests/testutils.sh"
profile_accept .
